From dd80c371d2bfebb261feb83853b7eee16157f471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:18:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a5xx: no fast clear after draws or of depth in
 forced sysmem

The a5xx fast clear (a BLIT event, made for GMEM) is not ordered after the
batch's earlier draws in bypass rendering: draw -> clear kept the draw's
pixels, even after a finish. A depth clear at the start of a batch let a
later depth test fail once in four runs. With FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem, clear
those with u_blitter (a draw); a color clear before any draw keeps the
fast clear, which behaved in every run.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

Task 24 stage 2: counts fast clears and u_blitter clears (after a draw, or
of depth/stencil) for SWEETCA_DRAWPROF.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
index 493121f..e0ce8f0 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
@@ -455,6 +455,24 @@ fd5_clear(struct fd_context *ctx, enum fd_buffer_mask buffers,
        is_z32(pfb->zsbuf.format))
       return false;
 
+   /* ios-jasmine: the fast clear is a BLIT event, made for GMEM. In forced
+    * sysmem (bypass) rendering it is not ordered after this batch's earlier
+    * draws: draw -> clear left the draw's pixels in memory even after a
+    * finish (task 24 pixel gate, 2026-10-28, imported and GL-allocated color
+    * targets alike), and a depth clear at the start of a batch let a later
+    * depth test fail in one of four runs. Only a color clear before any draw
+    * of the batch behaved; everything else clears with a draw (u_blitter),
+    * which is ordered like any other draw.
+    */
+   if (FD_DBG(SYSMEM) &&
+       (ctx->batch->num_draws > 0 || (buffers & (FD_BUFFER_DEPTH | FD_BUFFER_STENCIL)))) {
+      /* Task 24 stage 2: how often CoreAnimation reaches this (SWEETCA_DRAWPROF). */
+      SWEET_EVENT(ctx->batch->num_draws > 0 ? SPE_CLEAR_BLIT_AFTER_DRAW : SPE_CLEAR_BLIT_ZS, 1);
+      return false;
+   }
+   if (FD_DBG(SYSMEM))
+      SWEET_EVENT(SPE_CLEAR_FAST, 1);
+
    fd5_emit_render_cntl(ctx, true, false);
 
    if (buffers & FD_BUFFER_COLOR) {
